title: Changes miscounts Role::Filters call sites as twelve; it is fourteen
updated: 2026-08-27T06:36:30Z
---

The Role::Filters paragraph in Changes under {{$NEXT}} says:

  '... applied at every one of the twelve call sites that accept a filters
  option (list and prune on containers, images, networks, volumes, secrets,
  configs and plugins, plus images->build_prune).'

That enumeration is 2 (containers) + 2 (images) + 2 (networks) + 2 (volumes)
+ 1 (secrets) + 1 (configs) + 1 (plugins) + 1 (build_prune) = 12, and grepping
_normalise_filters in lib/ finds 12 matching call sites plus two more the
sentence does not mention: images->search (Images.pm) and system->events
(System.pm). Both are real, both are correctly wired (client->_normalise_filters
called, and each method's own POD says so -- 'Shape-checked and normalised by
L<API::Docker::Role::Filters>' appears on both), so this is not a functional
gap. It is the summary sentence in Changes undercounting by two and omitting
two of the fourteen call sites from its own list -- 'every ... call site' is
therefore not quite true as written.

'eight resource classes' in the same paragraph is correct (containers, images,
networks, volumes, secrets, configs, plugins, system all `with` the role).

Fix: twelve -> fourteen, and add images->search and system->events to the
parenthetical list. No code change.

Found during the pre-release audit; not fixed here per the audit's own scope
(report only).
